# Google Sheets — where form submissions are written.
#
# Setup:
#   1. In Google Cloud, create a project and enable the Google Sheets API.
#   2. Create a service account and download its JSON key.
#   3. Create the spreadsheet in the CLIENT'S Google account, with two tabs
#      named exactly "Enquiries" and "Partners".
#   4. Share that spreadsheet with the service account email, as Editor.
#      Skipping this step is the usual cause of a 403 on append.
#   5. Copy the values below into .env.local, and into Vercel's env settings.

GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=your-service-account@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com

# Paste the whole private_key value from the JSON key, quoted, keeping the \n
# escapes exactly as they appear in the file.
GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIIE...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# The long id in the sheet URL:
# https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/THIS_PART/edit
SHEET_ID=
